WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.731
so as we were going into production for yesterday's
show, Robert Mueller spoke, Robert Mueller

00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:11.009
issued a statement, he spoke publicly for
the first time since the publication of the

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:17.840
Mueller report and it very quickly became
a braking and major story in and of itself,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.880
but also because of the reactions that it
triggered from President Donald Trump himself

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.960
from Fox news anchor, Bret Baier, all of which
we'll get to a little bit later.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.070
But the bottom line is that it was announced
yesterday that Robert Mueller would be issuing

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.180
a statement special prosecutor.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.590
He ended, uh, indeed did issue that statement.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:43.140
He spoke publicly and he confirmed that he
could not clear and has not cleared President

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.890
Donald Trump of criminal wrongdoing.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:45.890
Period.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:52.500
Now, a lot of my audience hopefully read the
Mueller report and if you read the molar report,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.780
nothing that Robert Mueller said yesterday
would come as a surprise to those who were

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.600
operating on the basis of what the bar letter
said.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:06.440
For example, anyone who fell for no collusion,
no obstruction, uh, if you bought into that

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.640
narrative, then when Robert Mueller yesterday
said, if we could have cleared Trump, we would

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.850
have cleared Trump.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.580
Meaning we didn't clear Trump because we couldn't
clear Trump.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.300
That may have actually been newsworthy to
you.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:24.790
Robert Mueller saying, if we had confidence
the president did not commit a crime, we would

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:25.790
have said.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:26.790
So.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:31.159
The reason the report doesn't clear Trump
of obstruction of justice is because Robert

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:34.810
Mueller could not clear Trump of obstruction
of justice.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:40.510
And then again, Robert Mueller pointing out
that the Justice Department won't charge Trump,

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:45.720
but that there are other options again referring
to impeachment and many Democrats, uh, as

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.040
a result of Robert Mueller's statement yesterday
saying, now it is time to start that impeachment

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.800
debate on the floor of the house.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.910
But we will get to that a little context for
what Robert Mueller said.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:02:02.450
When a subject of an investigation obstructs
that investigation or lives to investigators,

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.860
it strikes at the core of their government's
effort to find the truth and hold wrongdoers

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.450
accountable.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:13.280
Let me say a word about the report.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.950
The report has two parts addressing the two
main issues.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:24.180
We were asked to investigate the first volume
of the report details numerous efforts emanating

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.350
from Russia to influence the election.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:33.800
His volume includes a discussion of the Trump
campaign's response to this activity as well

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:41.060
as our conclusion that there was insufficient
evidence to charge a broader conspiracy.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:46.930
And in the second volume the report describes
the results and analysis of our obstruction

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:54.349
of justice investigation involving the president
and the order appointing me as special council

00:02:54.349 --> 00:03:00.560
authorized us to investigate actions that
could obstruct the investigation.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.540
We conducted that investigation and we kept
the office of the acting attorney general

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:13.150
apprised of the progress of our work and as
set forth in the report after that investigation,

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:18.090
if we had had con confidence that the president
clearly did not commit a crime, we would have

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.090
said so.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:23.490
Mueller also announced that he's retiring,
resigned, resigning his position as special

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:29.840
prosecutor retiring from the Justice Department,
sort of very formally ending his role as special

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.840
prosecutor.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.680
So on the one hand, major breaking news, special
counsel saying, I can't clear Trump.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.410
On the other hand, nothing's surprising at
all.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:43.110
If you read the Mueller report, uh, if instead
of listening to the William Barr or to Trump

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:48.750
or Trump's kids or Fox News or Sean Hannity,
you would know already that the president

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.000
was not cleared of obstruction by Mueller's
investigation.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:59.170
Bottom line, in all likelihood, Donald Trump
committed the crime, multiple counts of obstruction

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.290
of justice.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:06.910
Robert Mueller did not indict, uh, for political
reasons, for technical reasons, pointing out

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:13.330
that the Justice Department has this policy
of not inditing sitting presidents, but pointing

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:17.189
out again, that there are other remedies available.

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:23.569
Uh, and there are some who are interpreting
this as a signal from Robert Mueller to Nancy

00:04:23.569 --> 00:04:29.990
Pelosi to whoever that might be in a position
to actually deal with impeachment seriously.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.389
That is the only path forward if you want
to hold Trump accountable for what appears

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:40.210
to be, uh, um, uh, obstruction on, from my
recollection of the Mueller report, eight

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:46.779
of 14 possible obstruct obstructive acts,
I believe is how they were referred to in

00:04:46.779 --> 00:04:47.779
the Mueller report.

00:04:47.779 --> 00:04:49.770
So on impeachment, there's some momentum here.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:53.419
There, there is a public statement from Robert
Mueller.

00:04:53.419 --> 00:04:54.740
People they're going to prison.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:56.529
Um, let's move forward.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:05:01.639
And I have been saying for awhile now that
there are numerous strategic benefits for

00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:05.430
Democrats to starting impeachment debate on
the floor of the house.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:09.840
I do not believe that you going to remove
Trump, but I am going to outline later on

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.650
in the program what the advantages to doing
this would be.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:13.990
And I think they're, they, they are clear.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:18.349
I know that there is a contingent of the left
which says, you know, it could backfire if

00:05:18.349 --> 00:05:21.749
Democrats start impeachment proceedings on
the floor of the house.

00:05:21.749 --> 00:05:24.599
It could reinvigorate Trump's base.

00:05:24.599 --> 00:05:30.770
It could be a distraction from 2020 Democratic
candidates talking about ideas and policy.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.349
Uh, I don't believe that.

00:05:32.349 --> 00:05:35.819
And I'm going to outline that for you a little
bit on in the program.

00:05:35.819 --> 00:05:37.439
Start the impeachment debate.

00:05:37.439 --> 00:05:42.789
Get things going, get testimony from witnesses,
expose the content of the Mueller report to

00:05:42.789 --> 00:05:47.860
the American people, which as I told you yesterday
and the day before and the day before that

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.169
most Americans have not read the molar report.

00:05:50.169 --> 00:05:52.500
Most Americans don't understand what is in
the molar report.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:57.210
Uh, and it would be extremely beneficial to
get that out in front of as many Americans

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.210
as possible.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:04.919
And by the way, side note, Mueller and his
statement also did again say Russia was working

00:06:04.919 --> 00:06:09.289
through wikileaks for the publication of a
lot of the stuff that ultimately was published

00:06:09.289 --> 00:06:11.500
that was illegally obtained by Russia.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:17.050
Um, that is something that people on the right
and left, we're denying for years, which Mueller

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.759
has now repeated and provided evidence for
in his report.

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:24.749
Not a peep, not a peep from all the people
who said there's no way wikileaks would ever

00:06:24.749 --> 00:06:26.589
be involved in anything like that.

00:06:26.589 --> 00:08:00.269
Oh, well they were, they were.

